{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1459621-traditional-ftl","id":1459621,"title":"Traditional FTL","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-10T22:02:17-07:00","id":1459621,"title":"Traditional FTL","content":"Now obviiously in Canon, we don't have it. but what impact would say a star trek style FTL drive have on the setting?<br /> <br /> On the one hand, all but the highest end of Star Trek style drives are far slower than either Nova warping or Psion teleports, on the other hand, for shorter ranges, they avoid the need for, well, a psion or nova. <br /> <br /> So how would they work, what would the impact be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T23:07:16-07:00","id":1459624,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s perfectly possible that Novas have built a Novatech Warp Drive, but if there is any one operating it is not under Aeon watch, so, maybe a Aberrant era colony have one\u2026<br /> <br /> As far it works too far away from Earth or any important colony nothing changes, except for local transportation.<br /> <br /> A ship that takes a few minutes to reach Mars instead of days, and a week or so to get to a nearby colony would be useful but only to local transport, imagining you have a limited number of Teleporters, and they would not be around taking a few tons of material from here to there for a absurd amount of money.<br /> <br /> But if you think you may take a few years from Earth to some colonies, it start to make little sense, because in a few years the chance of a Teleporter shows up and take you in seconds is high.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think there would be any big change in the setting, except for maybe the accessibility of a few near by (in the galactic scale) colonies during the absence of the teleporters, but it would not be that significant in the macro view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T13:11:26-07:00","id":1459683,"title":"","content":"I think their biggest impact would be for planetary travel inside a single solar system. Though I think that impact would be huge, especially for Aberrant era. Even for Aeon era it would be pretty big for stellar mining and colonization efforts as resources could constantly be traveling back and forth without the need of a teleporter of which there are only a couple thousand at most between all the Orders. With Warp style FTL companies and governments could keep a constant stream of commerce and supplies and travel going. While still limited by terraforming speeds, I think Mars would grow very fast.<br /> <br /> The usefulness of FTL goes up even more in Aberrant era where they are just starting the space exploration and colonizing efforts as there are so few space capable Novas. While not as fast or effective as teleportation or portals, it would be a lot more convenient for humanity as a whole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T20:00:17-07:00","id":1459716,"title":"","content":"The usefulness of FTL is also dependent on the speed, reliability, and resource consumption of the ships. According to the old GURPS Prime Directive sourcebook, even civilian freighters in the Captain Kirk era could cruise nearly 5 parsecs/day, and Alpha Centauri is slightly over a parsec from Earth. A civilian hauler should be able to make the trip in about 32 hours. Add in time for docking/undocking and loading/unloading, and I could see them making a round trip each week. That puts them way ahead of modern cargo ships.<br /> <br /> Next Gen era ships would be much faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T06:06:50-07:00","id":1459744,"title":"","content":"Like you said, it would allow baselines/neutrals to engage in interstellar travel without Inspired assistance.<br /> <br /> I could see a post-Aeon setting that gradually grows into something resembling the Star Trek Federation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T06:33:40-07:00","id":1459746,"title":"","content":"On a side step in the question, I think if the tech needed for a warpdrives was invented by a Talent, it would not be considered unnatural by the general population, as talents are not really supernatural in the setting context. Pretty sure a guy like Cochrane would be a Talent in TC.<br /> <br /> Another sidestep, thinking the Psionic FTL travel is similar to Battlestar Galactica Jump drive (it disappear and appear in another place), and Warp (the main Nova FTL system) is similar to Star Wars Hyperdrive (you open a hole in space, jump in it, travel though it and emerge in the other side). We could say Talent FTL travel is similar to Warp drive, that is basically traveling faster than light by just moving faster than light, without leaving the space or breaking its continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T06:58:09-07:00","id":1459749,"title":"","content":"Something I wrote awhile back<br /> <br /> Pseudo science of skip drive.<br /> Using the tech of the skip suit alone has destroyed all test craft trying to exceed the speed of light. It seems that the mass does not skip so well when it increases through relativistic speed. Though with the use of a cheat drive that lowers objects subjective mass and inertia the ship is actually able to skim the surface of spacetime. With the power available through the ZP cell, we have been able to boost the skip of space time to a stable observed speed of 1 light year per hour. Though the technology still has potentially more speed, the techs busy trying to master what we have accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T08:52:31-07:00","id":1459753,"title":"","content":"Different forms of interstellar travel create interesting strategic issues and good hooks for stories. <br /> <br /> If non-inspired FTL was a gate and jump system, then key points in the various star-systems become vital choke points. Certain star-systems would have more jump points than others and would become natural trade hubs. This would make non-inspired FTL analogous to oceanic travel and trade. Inspired FTL would be more like air travel.<br /> <br /> There would be complex political, economic, and social, consequences to such a system. The stories would show up in flocks.<br /> <br /> Another tack might be to make inspired FTL travel cheap and fast, but seriously restricted in some way. Clipper ships compared to non-inspired FTL. So if you have to get it there quickly and in volume, use non-inspired FTL. If you want to explore off the beaten path, use inspired FTL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-12-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T14:12:37-07:00","id":1459766,"title":"","content":"Beyond trading, the other major use of mundane FTL ships would be war. Using Psion or Aberrant powers/tech for space travel creates severe transport bottlenecks, while a fleet of warships and troop transports can get everyone to the invasion site at the same time. No need to hold a portal open for hours while troops trickle through a hole in the universe and the enemy does everything they can to destroy the beachhead site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T15:32:00-07:00","id":1459777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1459621-traditional-ftl?p=1459766#post1459766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond trading, the other major use of mundane FTL ships would be war. Using Psion or Aberrant powers/tech for space travel creates severe transport bottlenecks, while a fleet of warships and troop transports can get everyone to the invasion site at the same time. No need to hold a portal open for hours while troops trickle through a hole in the universe and the enemy does everything they can to destroy the beachhead site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But I still say, make the rules of the two types of transport different. So that each has pragmatic advantages and troublesome restrictions. That makes for problems that will need resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T19:04:39-07:00","id":1459806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1459621-traditional-ftl?p=1459766#post1459766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond trading, the other major use of mundane FTL ships would be war. Using Psion or Aberrant powers/tech for space travel creates severe transport bottlenecks, while a fleet of warships and troop transports can get everyone to the invasion site at the same time. No need to hold a portal open for hours while troops trickle through a hole in the universe and the enemy does everything they can to destroy the beachhead site.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This got me thinking, both could be used in tandem. The use of local ships could hold off enemy ships while the allies from what would be too far away normally to get there in time with slower warp drive ftl use a portal to funnel ships in to a few thousand miles or so away to keep them protected from enemies and then they can use there warp drives to fly in and join their comrades. Might not be the most efficient but it does prevent enemies from targeting a single bottleneck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T02:08:44-07:00","id":1459828,"title":"","content":"Piracy! <br /> <br /> Point-to-point teleportation means that the ship/cargo can't be intercepted &quot;midway&quot;, since there is no midway. Going from place to place really really fast means that someone probably could do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}